 <office:master-styles>
  <style:master-page style:name="Standard" style:page-layout-name="pm1" draw:style-name="dp1"/>
 </office:master-styles>
 <office:body>
  <office:text text:use-soft-page-breaks="true">
   <text:sequence-decls>
    <text:sequence-decl text:display-outline-level="0" text:name="Illustration"/>
    <text:sequence-decl text:display-outline-level="0" text:name="Table"/>
    <text:sequence-decl text:display-outline-level="0" text:name="Text"/>
    <text:sequence-decl text:display-outline-level="0" text:name="Drawing"/>
    <text:sequence-decl text:display-outline-level="0" text:name="Figure"/>
   </text:sequence-decls>
   <text:h text:style-name="P3" text:outline-level="3">Previously </text:h>
   <text:list xml:id="list3023624204" text:style-name="L1">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P7"><text:span text:style-name="T3">P</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T2">arty was informed by Prof. Plaarg that Rosie and her party had not returned from their excursion into the Lorehold excavation site.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P8">Party went into the site to discover what became of Rosie</text:p>
     <text:list>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P9">Met with a slew of monsters guarding the main room hidden away at the end of the dig</text:p>
       <text:list>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="P9">Gelatinous cubes (3x), Ankhegs (6x), Casme (2x) and a Green Slaad</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="P9">Room appears to be some kind of alter (DC 14 Investigation: really a casting room for larger effect spells, DC 18 Investigation: like the Gate currently open)</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
      </text:list-item>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P9">Party managed to avoid all trapped rooms (yaaaaaay)</text:p>
      </text:list-item>
     </text:list>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P10"><text:span text:style-name="T2">Party vanquished the enemies inside the alter room, </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T4">all of Rosie’s party are safe, healing, but still unconscious (DC 14 Arcana/Medicine: Magically put to sleep, only to awake after a predetermined amount of time has passed).</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P1"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P4" text:outline-level="3">Currently</text:h>
   <text:list xml:id="list130025478855739" text:continue-numbering="true" text:style-name="L1">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P11"><text:span text:style-name="T2">Gate is still open for the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T6">moment, set a timer for 7 minutes IRL to allow party to attempt to investigate the Gate before it closes on them. If anyone attempts to pass through the Gate, they must succeed on a </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T8">DC 2</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T9">8</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T8"> WIS Save</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T6"> or be charmed into walking away from the Gate.</text:span></text:p>
     <text:list>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P12">There is no physical structure to the Gate, it looks like a “tear in reality with burning edges to it”</text:p>
      </text:list-item>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P11"><text:span text:style-name="T6">On the other side of the Gate is The Abyss, </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T7">specifically a murky river (Maelstrom River, leads to plane of Limbo but many demons along the way) covered in various demons.</text:span></text:p>
      </text:list-item>
     </text:list>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P13">Party can search the Green Slaad’s robe pockets, inside is a slip of parchment covered in strange symbols (Language is Abyssal, ask what languages party understands). </text:p>
     <text:list>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P13">Even if someone is able to read it, only some of the writing is readable (as much of it hasn’t been written at this time yet/Azetoph shenanigans).</text:p>
       <text:list>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="P13">Party can make out, “Bring the students along the Maelstrom River, to the mouth of Cave Cacophony. The guards will let you pass.” The rest of the message is amorphous, constantly changing Abyssal letters.</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
      </text:list-item>
     </text:list>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P16"><text:span text:style-name="T6">Once timer goes off, Gate closes and anyone inside must succeed another </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T8">DC 28 WIS Save</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T10"> or be forced from The Abyss back to in front of the alter. Anyone trapped inside… is fully trapped in The Abyss.</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P14">Party will likely return to Plaarg, have an improvised discussion.</text:p>
     <text:list>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P14">At some point, after hearing the news the party wishes to share, Plaarg will say the following</text:p>
       <text:list>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="P16"><text:soft-page-break/><text:span text:style-name="T10">“We have, either at individual times or altogether, experienced The Feywild, The Nine Hells, Celeste’s Labyrinth, and now The Abyss… I must admit that this </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T11">is very much out of my area of expertise, I know close to nothing about the Planar-verse. We need an expert. I believe it is time we find our friend, the magical theoretician; we need John Crowley and we need him fast.”</text:span></text:p>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="P15">“Tenzington—I don’t suppose you are able to put out any feelers in your sphere of influence? Perhaps you know a contact whom might know a contact whom might know where to find our dear Crowley?”</text:p>
         <text:list>
          <text:list-item>
           <text:p text:style-name="P15">“I can certainly ask around. A man as renowned as Crowley was just some years back, someone must know something.”</text:p>
          </text:list-item>
         </text:list>
        </text:list-item>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="P15">“In the meantime [to the Party], we will watch over Rosie and her party. Lisette and myself will personally attend to them, and ensure a speedy recovery.”</text:p>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
      </text:list-item>
     </text:list>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P2"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P5" text:outline-level="3">Notes</text:h>
   <text:list xml:id="list3449126679" text:style-name="L2">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P18"><text:span text:style-name="T5">A</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T1">dam learns about Mira</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P18">Celeste goes to investigate Gate</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P19">Memories <text:span text:style-name="T12">across campus </text:span>can <text:span text:style-name="T12">be modified through amplification chambers</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P20">Tenzington is putting feelers out for Storm on the Horizon who might know where John Crowley is.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P21">Mira does all kinds of Magic Mouth fuckery with the party, makes Perry’s shoes Squidward walk and Perry’s dorm door yodel.</text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P21">Perry brings his yodeling door to Quentillius’s dorm</text:p>
     <text:list>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P22">He swaps his door for Quent’s</text:p>
      </text:list-item>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P17"><text:span text:style-name="T13">His (now Prismari) door does not match the Quandrix dormitory</text:span></text:p>
      </text:list-item>
     </text:list>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
   <text:p text:style-name="P23"/>
   <text:h text:style-name="P6" text:outline-level="3">Next</text:h>
   <text:list xml:id="list1898633072" text:style-name="L3">
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P24"><text:span text:style-name="T14">Party is going to meet up with </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T15">Rosie and her party for an overview on rules for Mage Tower, as well as run through some scrimmages</text:span></text:p>
    </text:list-item>
    <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="P25">Celeste has her Student Mages of Faith meeting</text:p>
     <text:list>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P25">Shuvadri will come up to converse with her</text:p>
       <text:list>
        <text:list-item>
         <text:p text:style-name="P25">Will mention some Witherbloom students who worship Pharika, Goddess of Affliction</text:p>
         <text:list>
          <text:list-item>
           <text:p text:style-name="P25">They will know of several Pharika nunneries throughout the land, one of which currently houses John Crowley and <text:span text:style-name="T16">also Celeste’s friend, Jael.</text:span></text:p>
          </text:list-item>
         </text:list>
        </text:list-item>
       </text:list>
      </text:list-item>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P26"><text:soft-page-break/>Shuvadri herself is a worshiper of [[THEROS GOD HERE]]</text:p>
      </text:list-item>
      <text:list-item>
       <text:p text:style-name="P27">Will try to explain to Celeste, that she must reconnect herself to Karametra in order to find inner piece. She would be happy to sit in prayer to their respective gods.</text:p>
      </text:list-item>
     </text:list>
    </text:list-item>
   </text:list>
  </office:text>
 </office:body>
</office:document>